 (Qwen scaling): FAIL - IFR/ACDC degenerate\n- plan_008 (Size-controlled baseline): 76% of IOI advantage from selection quality (not size)\n- plan_009 (Bootstrap CIs): Partial (IOI/SVA/FR done)\n\n### Configuration Files\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/min_necessary_circuit_css/artifacts/phase2_configs.yaml`\n\n**Summary:** Comprehensive Phase 2 experiment matrix with 18 experiments spanning:\n- **GPT-2 Small** (3 tasks × 3 methods): IOI, Greater-than, Docstring (EAP-IG, Edge Pruning, ACDC)\n- **Qwen-0.5B** (4 tasks × 3 methods): IOI, Greater-than, Docstring, IOI-variant (EAP-IG, EP, IFR)\n- **Gemma-2 2B** (4 tasks × 3 methods): Same tasks as Qwen\n- **Llama-3.1 8B** (4 tasks × 3 methods): Same tasks, higher GPU budgets\n\nBinarization strategies defined per-method:\n- EAP-IG: topn (n=200)\n- Edge Pruning: threshold (t=0.5)\n- ACDC/IFR: unique_score_rank or threshold\n\n### Analysis & Results Files\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/min_necessary_circuit_css/artifacts/analysis/analysis_results.json`\n\n**Summary:** Cross-tabulation and circuit discovery analysis for GPT-2 IOI (K=3):\n- **Methods:** ACDC (254 edges), EAP-IG (200), Edge Pruning (252)\n- **Pairwise Jaccard:** 0.279 (ACDC vs EAP-IG), 0.307 (ACDC vs EP), 0.284 (EAP-IG vs EP)\n- **CSS results:** 49 edges agreed (all in), 388 off-diagonal (88.8%)\n- **CIRCUS tiers:** 10 stable core, 36 method-specific, 39 cross-unstable, 415 noise\n- **ACDC sensitivity sweep:** τ=[0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1, 0.3] with off-diagonal % increasing to 95.3%\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/min_necessary_circuit_css/artifacts/mvp_arithmetic_gpt2_k3/report/mean_ablation_results.json`\n\n**Summary:** Zero vs mean ablation comparison on Arithmetic:\n- Zero ablation: EAP-IG CPR=-0.131, EP=-0.163, ACDC=-0.184, CSS=1.0=-0.184\n- Mean ablation: EAP-IG CPR=0.960, EP=0.918, ACDC=0.985, CSS=1.0=0.985\n- CSS=1.0 edges identical to ACDC top edges (CPR parity)\n\n### Dream/Imagined Results\n\n**Directory:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/min_necessary_circuit_css/artifacts/dream_reports/`\n\nThree completed dream reports (dream_20260513T054654, T081242, T092135) with tiered imagined experiments:\n\n**dream_20260513T092135/best/imagined_experiments.yaml** (Latest, EMNLP submission version):\n- 5 completed experiments imagined with detailed expected results:\n  1. **GPT-2 Factual Recall K=3 (plan_004):** FAIL expected (Jaccard=0.62 > 0.5 threshold)\n  2. **IOI Size-Controlled Baseline (plan_008):** 76.3% advantage retained (selection quality effect)\n  3. **Bootstrap CIs (plan_009):** IOI Δ=0.085 [CI 0.035-0.138, p=0.002], SVA crosses zero, FR significantly negative\n  4. **Zero vs Mean Ablation (plan_011):** CSS advantage robust (mean: Δ=0.065, 81.3% of zero advantage retained)\n  5. **IFR vs ACDC vs Gradient Divergence Analysis (plan_012):** Documents component-level scoring failure mechanistically\n  6. **Jaccard-CSS Diagnostic Scatter (plan_013):** 5/6 accuracy (Spearman ρ=-0.9, p=0.037 excluding outlier)\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT 2: solver-trace-ablation\n\n### Experiment Plans\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\n**Summary:** 12 planned experiments (P0/P1/P2 priority):\n\n**P0 (13 GPU hours, must-run headline results):**\n- plan_001: FOL single-logic GRPO, execution-only reward (500 steps, K=8, 3 seeds)\n- plan_002: FOL single-logic GRPO, execution+STA reward (full STA, 500 steps, 3 seeds)\n- plan_003: FOL held-out evaluation comparing plan_001 vs plan_002 using STA metrics\n- plan_004: STA O(1) vs O(N) ablation (negative result documentation)\n- plan_005: STA reward weight ablation (α/β ratios: 0.3/0.7, 0.5/0.5, 0.7/0.3)\n\n**P1 (8 GPU hours, completeness):**\n- plan_006-007: Prolog single-logic + multi-logic GRPO\n- plan_008: Cross-logic transfer evaluation\n- plan_009: SFT baseline comparison\n- plan_012: Hacking characterization (200 outputs manual annotation)\n\n**P2 (9 GPU hours, nice-to-have):**\n- plan_010: SMT-LIB single-logic GRPO\n- plan_011: Qwen3-8B scaling test\n\n### Reward Configurations\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/artifacts/grpo_exec_only.yaml`\n\n**Summary:** Baseline GRPO config (execution-only reward):\n- Model: Qwen3-4B\n- Reward: execution_only (exec_weight=1.0, sta_weight=0.0)\n- Training: 100 steps, per_device_batch_size=4, num_generations=4\n- Learning rate: 1.0e-6\n- Solver: prover9\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/artifacts/grpo_exec_sta.yaml`\n\n**Summary:** STA-enhanced GRPO config (execution + trace ablation reward):\n- Model: Qwen3-4B\n- Reward: execution_sta (exec_weight=0.5, sta_weight=0.5 — balanced weighting)\n- Training: 100 steps, same batch/generation settings\n- Learning rate: 1.0e-6\n- Solver: prover9\n\n### Dream/Imagined Results\n\n**Directory:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/artifacts/dream_reports/`\n\nOne in-progress dream report (dream_20260513T215750):\n- Status: imagining (actively generating imagined experiments)\n- Focus: MVP finding that full STA (O(N)) works as training signal but O(1) approximation ineffective (negative result)\n- Paper positioning: STA as methodology transfer (RIP → RL reward design), not novel algorithm\n- Two core claims: STA methodology + multi-logic empirical findings\n\n---\n\n## Supporting Files\n\n**Dream Registry Files:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/min_necessary_circuit_css/dream_registry.yaml` — 3 completed dream reports (T054654, T081242, T092135), 1 failed (T044816)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/dream_registry.yaml` — 1 in-progress dream (T215750)\n\n**Key Metadata:**\n- Venue targets: EMNLP 2026 Findings (min_nece